   "phases": [
    {
     "t": "Three weeks of waiting",
     "text": "After the first battle Brutus held the strong position, with the fleet supplying him; the triumvirs, short of food in an autumn plain, needed a decision. Antony pushed troops south and east past Cassius' old camp to threaten Brutus' communications, and Brutus extended his line of forts southward to match. Plutarch and Appian say Brutus' officers and Cassius' former soldiers, restless and unwilling to be thought afraid, forced him to offer battle on 23 October 42, which was exactly what his enemies wanted.",
