     "t": "Brutus' wing advances; the other is outflanked",
     "text": "Brutus led his own wing forward and drove back the troops opposite. Plutarch says the other wing, stretched thin to avoid being outflanked, was taken in the flank by Antony's men and broken, and that this happened because Cassius' veterans did not fight with conviction.",
