    {
     "t": "The Persian right is caught",
     "text": "On the second day, after the morning exchange of archery, the Persian right attacked Bouzes' cavalry, who gave ground. Pharas' 300 Heruli, posted at their own suggestion behind the hill on the left, came out and fell on the Persian rear, and Sunicas and Aigan's Huns charged in from the angle. The Persian right broke and lost about 3,000 men.",
