    {
     "t": "The Persian left cut in two",
     "text": "Belisarius and Hermogenes now sent Sunicas and Aigan's Huns across from the left angle to join Simmas and Ascan, together with many of Belisarius' own guardsmen, and threw them at the flank of the advancing Persian left. It was cut in two. Sunicas killed Baresmanes' standard-bearer and then Baresmanes himself, and 5,000 Persians died. The Roman commanders stopped the pursuit short, fearing a rally. Procopius notes that it was the first Persian defeat in battle in a long time.",
