    {
     "t": "Totila plays for time",
     "text": "Totila was waiting for 2,000 horsemen under Teias. To delay, he rode out alone between the armies in gilded armour with purple streamers, and performed a display of horsemanship, throwing his lance in the air and catching it, wheeling his horse. Procopius notes that the Romans had eaten while standing in their ranks; the Goths went back to their camp for a meal when the reinforcements arrived, and Totila changed into the armour of an ordinary soldier.",
