    {
     "t": "Recoil and rout",
     "text": "Late in the day the Gothic cavalry broke and fell back onto its own infantry, which was carried away in the flight. The Roman line advanced and the 1,000 horsemen worked round behind. About 6,000 Goths died. Totila escaped with a few companions but was overtaken and mortally wounded by the Gepid Asbad, and died at Caprae; Procopius also records a version in which he was hit by an arrow early in the battle. Narses had the Lombards, who burned houses and raped women on the way, sent home with an escort. Teias, elected king, was killed at Mons Lactarius in October.",
