    {
     "t": "Into the ravine",
     "text": "The Roman infantry was pushed west into the angle of the ravines. With the bridge held, there was no way out: the Arabic tradition says that many were killed or fell into the Wadi al-Ruqqad, giving the name al-Waqusa to the scene. Theodore Trithyrios was killed; Vahan's fate is uncertain. The date usually given is August 636. Heraclius, at Antioch, is said to have bidden farewell to Syria ('Peace unto thee, Syria, and what an excellent country this is for the enemy') and withdrew to Constantinople. Jerusalem surrendered in 637 or 638.",
